{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC self-contradiction found while implementing and corrected: AC1 demanded exactly one 'def _shadow' under src/rebar while AC3 demanded _lib_ops._shadow stay unchanged - both cannot hold, since leaving _lib_ops' definition in place leaves two. Resolved by consolidating all FOUR sites rather than three: emit_shadow_snapshot already declares repo_root: ... | None = None (_operation_config.py:225), so passing repo_root=None is byte-identical to omitting it and a single _shadow(surface, repo_root=None) serves the three MCP twins and the library variant alike. _lib_ops' call sites move from positional _shadow(repo_root, surface) to _shadow(surface, repo_root=repo_root). _config_resolvers._positive_int remains genuinely out of scope - it returns a default instead of raising, so merging it into the argparse converter would turn a rejected CLI value into a silent default."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787372722064125001,"uuid":"24317cbd-e634-4ea7-8fe6-885bc2a42ade"}